    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d222">

                <pb facs="0384" n="270" xml:id="pg270"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.00R296/4590½</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Telephone Conversation</hi><anchor
                        n="83" xml:id="d222-f1"/></head>
                <dateline>
                    <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-head" calendar="gregorian"
                        type="conversation-or-meeting-date" when="1931-07-17T10:15:00+01:00">July
                        17, 1931, 10:15 a.m.</date>
                </dateline>
                <p>Mr. Atherton said that the meeting at London had been definitely set for 6 P.M.
                    on Monday.<anchor n="84" xml:id="d222-f2"/> The Secretary told Atherton that it
                    should be clearly understood in London that Henderson had fully agreed to the
                    suggestion that the Germans come to Paris first and that everyone here in Paris
                    felt that this was desirable.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d222-f1" n="83" type="source" xml:id="d222-f1-content">
                <p>Between the Secretary of State in Paris and Mr. Ray Atherton, Counselor of
                    Embassy in London, July 17, 1931, 10:15 a.m.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d222-f2" n="84" xml:id="d222-f2-content">
                <p>July 20.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
